<title>USA: U.S. July factory orders rose 1.8 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. July factory orders rose 1.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce seasonally adjusted data on U.S. factory orders, shipments and unfilled orders.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    July-Rev from    June--Rev from   May</p>
<p> New Orders		  1.8		 -0.7   -0.9	2.3</p>
<p> -Ex-Transportation	2.1		 -0.6   -0.8	0.7</p>
<p> -Ex-Defense		 2.8		 -1.2   -1.6	2.3</p>
<p> NonDurables Orders	1.8		 -1.2   -1.3	0.3</p>
<p> Durables Orders	   1.7    1.6	-0.2   -0.2	4.2</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders   7.6    7.2	-4.6   -4.6     11.1</p>
<p> -Ex-Aircraft, Parts     4.2    3.6	 2.6    2.5     -0.3</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders    -36.7  -36.5	26.4   26.4	6.2</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    July-Rev from    June--Rev from   May</p>
<p> Durables NonDefense     3.6    3.5	-1.2   -1.2	4.1</p>
<p> Total Shipments	   1.2		 -0.8   -1.0	1.0</p>
<p> Durables Shipments	0.8    0.7	-0.3   -0.4	1.7</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders   1.0		  0.7    0.6	0.6</p>
<p> Unfilled Durables	 1.0    1.0	 0.7    0.7	0.6</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast a 1.0 percent rise in total factory orders for July.  </p>
<p>    In Blns of Dlrs:   July--Rev from   June--Rev from    May</p>
<p> New Orders	     317.63	     312.14  311.22   314.19</p>
<p> -Ex-Transportation   276.04	     270.38  269.65   271.90</p>
<p> -Ex-Defense	    312.50	     304.03  302.76   307.78</p>
<p> NonDurables Orders   144.71	     142.15  142.04   143.91</p>
<p> Durables Orders	172.93  172.65   169.99  169.99   170.29</p>
<p> NonDef. Cap Orders    46.18   46.02    42.92   42.91    44.98</p>
<p> -Ex-Aircraft, Parts   38.94   38.71    37.39   37.35    36.45</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders     5.14    5.15     8.11    8.11     6.41</p>
