<p> Durables NonDefense  167.79  167.50   161.89  161.88   163.87</p>
<p> Total Shipments	312.67	     308.85  308.18   311.20</p>
<p> Durables Shipments   168.18  168.01   166.90  166.89   167.49</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders  504.16	     499.20  498.96   495.91</p>
<p> Unfilled Durables    480.15  480.05   475.40  475.41   472.31</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    July-Rev from    June-Rev from    May</p>
<p> Primary Metals	    1.0    2.1	-0.2   -0.7	2.0</p>
<p> Industrial Machinery    2.9    2.1	 0.3    0.2	1.2</p>
<p> Electrical Equipment    4.7    4.7	 3.8    3.9     -1.3</p>
<p> Transport Equipment    -0.4   Unch	-1.3   -1.2     14.6</p>
<p>    In Blns of Dlrs:   July--Rev from   June--Rev from    May</p>
<p> Primary Metals	  15.71   15.79    15.55   15.47    15.58</p>
<p> Industrial Machinery  32.61   32.30    31.69   31.65    31.60</p>
<p> Electrical Equipment  28.02   28.07    26.77   26.80    25.79</p>
<p> Transport Equipment   41.59   41.79    41.76   41.80    42.30</p>
<p>The July rise in total factory orders was the fourth monthly increase in the past five months.</p>
<p>The July inventories-to-shipments ratio fell to 1.39 from a revised 1.40 in June. The June ratio was previously reported at 1.41. The department reported initial data on July orders for durable goods on August 23.</p>
